CBSTM03A | enum | HTML-FIXED-LN: HTML-L01, HTML-L02, HTML-L03, HTML-L04, HTML-L05, HTML-L06, HTML-L07, HTML-L08, HTML-LTRS, HTML-LTRE, HTML-LTDS, HTML-LTDE, HTML-L10, HTML-L15, HTML-L16, HTML-L17, HTML-L18, HTML-L22-35, HTML-L30-42, HTML-L31, HTML-L43, HTML-L47, HTML-L48, HTML-L50, HTML-L51, HTML-L53, HTML-L54, HTML-L58, HTML-L61, HTML-L64, HTML-L75, HTML-L78, HTML-L79, HTML-L80 | 5 | HTML-FIXED-LN PIC X(100) is a line buffer: every use is SET HTML-Lnn TO TRUE then WRITE FD-HTMLFILE-REC FROM HTML-FIXED-LN (lines 439–454, 508–532, 536–600, 6000-WRITE-TRANS); no statement ever tests a condition-name ("checked in none"). It is a table of HTML text constants addressed by name, not a value the program chooses among. The rule is wrong (the key agrees: carddemo.scores lists it under not). Note the data-flow check T-E1 passes on it (only SETs store into it); what refutes it is T-E2 (never read). → T-E2. | T-E1, T-E2 | Fable
