CSUTLDTC | enum | FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE: FC-INVALID-DATE, FC-INSUFFICIENT-DATA, FC-BAD-DATE-VALUE, FC-INVALID-ERA, FC-UNSUPP-RANGE, FC-INVALID-MONTH, FC-BAD-PIC-STRING, FC-NON-NUMERIC-DATA, FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO | 55 | the 8-byte Language Environment condition token CEEDAYS hands back (X'0000...' is success; the others decode to severity 3, message numbers 0x09CB–0x09D9 = CEE2507–CEE2521, facility 'CEE'). The names cover the CEEDAYS feedback codes the authors chose; the EVALUATE has WHEN OTHER MOVE 'Date is invalid', so the authors expected values outside the list. Whether CEEDAYS can return any other token is IBM's documentation to settle (D-E2); no fixture runs CSUTLDTC (it is CALLed by online programs) and CEEDAYS is not in the corpus. → D-E2; T-E2 passes (tested in A000-MAIN) | D-E2, T-E2 | Fable
CSUTLDTC | function | A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT | 95 | a function only because CSUTLDTC is a subprogram that hands control back with EXIT PROGRAM; run on its own its main line would fall into A000-MAIN | T-F1, T-F2 | Opus
